cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FlyGuard: connectome-derived collision avoidance for robots"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the FlyWire connectome it is built from."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ami"
repository-code: "https://github.com/your-username/flyguard"
abstract: >-
  A looming detector and obstacle-avoidance controller whose synaptic weights
  are taken directly from the FlyWire FAFB v783 Drosophila connectome, with no
  training and no fitted parameters in the detection path. Includes a
  leaky-integrate-and-fire engine, a retinotopic T4/T5 encoder driven by real
  optical flow, ROS2 nodes, and both learned and classical baselines for
  comparison.
keywords:
  - connectome
  - robotics
  - collision avoidance
  - spiking neural networks
  - Drosophila
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
